      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:2:30:1",
      "text": [
        " الصَّائِمِ يَكْتَحِلُ قَالَ لَا بَأْسَ بِهِ لَيْسَ بِطَعَامٍ وَ لَا شَرَابٍ .",
        "عَلِيُّ بْنُ إِبْرَاهِيمَ عَنْ أَبِيهِ عَنِ ابْنِ أَبِي عُمَيْرٍ عَنْ سُلَيْمَانَ الْفَرَّاءِ عَنْ غَيْرِ وَاحِدٍ عَنْ أَبِي جَعْفَرٍ ( عليه السلام ) مِثْلَهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ali Bin Al Hakam, from Suleyman Al Fara’a, from Muhammad Bin Muslim, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> regarding the Fasting-one who applies Kohl (in the eyes). He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘There is no problem with it. It is neither a food nor a drink’.",
          "<span style=\"font-size: small\">Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Suleyman Al Fara’a, from someone else,</span> (It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> – similar to it."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. A number of our people have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Ali ibn al-Hakam from Sulayman al-Farra’ from Muhammad ibn Muslim who has said the following: “About a fasting person’s use of kohl (special powder for eye treatment) abu Ja’far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that it is not harmful, because it is not a drink or food.’” Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Sulayman al-Farra’ from more than one person who have narrated a similar Hadith from abu Ja’far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam. "
        ]
      }
    },
